Spec: Dto

Purpose:
  Own the wire contract of the `vynil-server` diagnostic API as plain serde DTOs: the JSON shapes
    ./server.rs serializes into HTTP responses — cluster inventory (@ClusterInfo with @NodeInfo and
    @StorageClassInfo), platform package inventory (@PackagesState with @PackageState), instance
    children with live state (@ChildWithState), redaction tallies (@ScrubStats), the currently
    unused anonymization envelope (@AnonymizedResponse) and the popularity tally (@PopularityContest
    with @JukeboxCategory). Pure data — no functions, no validation, no custom serde impls; every
    observable of this file is what serializing and deserializing these shapes produces. A reader
    must be able to regenerate the exact JSON payloads and the exact serde accept/reject boundary
    from this spec alone.

Owns:
  ./dto.rs

Depends on:
  @common::Children from /common/src/lib.rs — embedded by @ChildWithState.child; its
    `#[serde(rename_all = "camelCase")]` wire (`apiVersion`, `kind`, `name`, `namespace` with
    `kind` and `name` required) is specified by /common/src/lib.sdd and re-emitted unchanged inside
    this crate's payloads.
  @serde derives (@Serialize / @Deserialize), @serde_json::Value and @std::collections::BTreeMap —
    versions locked in /Cargo.lock.

Must:
  Serialize every struct with keys exactly equal to the snake_case Rust field names: `nodes`,
    `distribution`, `kubernetes_version`, `vynil_version`, `storage_classes`, `ingress_classes`;
    `name`, `roles`, `instance_type`, `arch`, `os`, `kubelet_version`; `name`, `provisioner`,
    `is_default`; `items`; `kind`, `namespace`, `name`, `package`, `tag`, `ready`; `child`, `state`;
    `distinct`, `occurrences`; `data`, `scrub_stats`; `jukeboxes`; `categories`. No container or
    field in the file carries any serde attribute — no `rename`, no `rename_all`, no
    `skip_serializing_if`, no `default`, no `deny_unknown_fields` — so nothing moves.
  Emit struct keys in field-declaration order, and keep @None @Option fields present as explicit
    `null` on serialize (no skip attribute exists); deserialization then accepts either an omitted
    or a `null` key for every @Option — a deserialize-then-reserialize cycle is stable only because
    serialization always re-emits the key.
  Nest @common::Children's camelCase wire inside @ChildWithState's snake_case envelope: `child` is
    the snake_case key, its value always renders `apiVersion` (and `namespace`) in camelCase — the
    only camelCase island in this file's payloads (see Tasks).
  Pass @ChildWithState.state through untyped: @Option<@serde_json::Value> with no schema, no
    inspection, any JSON tree survives unchanged.
  Serialize @PopularityContest deterministically: both @std::collections::BTreeMap levels
    (@PopularityContest.jukeboxes and @JukeboxCategory.categories) iterate in key order, so jukebox,
    category and package keys land alphabetically and the body is byte-stable whatever the builder's
    insertion order in ./collect/popularity_contest.rs.
  Keep counts integral: @u32 for the package counts inside @JukeboxCategory maps, @usize for
    @ScrubStats.distinct and @ScrubStats.occurrences; the locked @serde_json boundary rejects
    floats, negatives and numeric strings against them.
  Derive @Default for @ScrubStats only — all other DTOs must be built field-by-field — and note the
    field-name coupling: ./server.rs @add_scrub_header hardcodes the `X-Diag-Redactions` grammar
    `distinct={distinct};occurrences={occurrences}`, so renaming a field silently renames the header
    keys. The counters count redactions produced by ./anonymize.rs: @distinct is the number of
    distinct secret values that matched at least once, @occurrences the total replacements.
  Ship @AnonymizedResponse<@T> outbound-only: unlike every other DTO it derives no @Deserialize,
    and its @Debug / @Clone are derived bounds on @T; the wire object is `data` (the serialized @T)
    followed by `scrub_stats`, with no in-crate inbound counterpart. Nothing constructs it today
    (see Tasks).
  Contribute no schema to the cluster: no @schemars / @JsonSchema derive exists here, unlike
    @common::Children which carries @JsonSchema for its CRD-side duty; these shapes are
    server-HTTP-only.

Exposes:
  @ClusterInfo — struct, derives @Serialize / @Deserialize / @Debug / @Clone; fields in declaration
    order: @nodes → @Vec<@NodeInfo>, @distribution → @String, @kubernetes_version → @String,
    @vynil_version → @Option<@String>, @storage_classes → @Vec<@StorageClassInfo>,
    @ingress_classes → @Vec<@String>.
  @NodeInfo — same derives; @name → @String, @roles → @Vec<@String>, @instance_type →
    @Option<@String>, @arch → @Option<@String>, @os → @Option<@String>, @kubelet_version →
    @Option<@String>.
  @StorageClassInfo — same derives; @name → @String, @provisioner → @String, @is_default → @bool.
  @PackagesState — same derives; @items → @Vec<@PackageState>.
  @PackageState — same derives; @kind → @String (free-form discriminator; the `ServiceInstance` /
    `SystemInstance` literals come from ./collect/packages.rs and are not validated here),
    @namespace → @String, @name → @String, @package → @String, @tag → @Option<@String>,
    @ready → @bool.
  @ChildWithState — same derives; @child → @common::Children, @state → @Option<@serde_json::Value>.
  @ScrubStats — same four derives plus @Default (@distinct and @occurrences start at `0`);
    @distinct → @usize, @occurrences → @usize.
  @AnonymizedResponse<@T> — generic struct, derives @Serialize / @Debug / @Clone only;
    @data → @T, @scrub_stats → @ScrubStats.
  @PopularityContest — struct, derives @Serialize / @Deserialize / @Debug / @Clone; @jukeboxes →
    @std::collections::BTreeMap<@String, @JukeboxCategory> keyed by `JuKebox` name.
  @JukeboxCategory — same derives; @categories →
    @std::collections::BTreeMap<@String, @std::collections::BTreeMap<@String, @u32>>, category →
    package → instance count.
  Full file surface: the ten types above are all @pub, reachable outside the crate because
    /server/src/lib.rs declares `pub mod dto;`; in-crate consumers are ./server.rs (JSON bodies and
    the `X-Diag-Redactions` header) and the ./collect/ builders.

Accepts:
  Deserialization input per struct is one JSON object over the frozen keys; required keys are the
    non-@Option fields: @ClusterInfo `nodes`, `distribution`, `kubernetes_version`,
    `storage_classes`, `ingress_classes`; @NodeInfo `name`, `roles`; @StorageClassInfo all three keys;
    @PackagesState `items`; @PackageState `kind`, `namespace`, `name`, `package`, `ready`;
    @ChildWithState `child` — whose @Children object itself requires camelCase `kind` and `name` —
    with `state` optional; @ScrubStats `distinct` and `occurrences`; @PopularityContest `jukeboxes`;
    @JukeboxCategory `categories`. No inbound JSON at all parses as @AnonymizedResponse.
  Unknown keys are dropped silently at every nesting level; a JSON object repeating one struct field
    key is rejected as a duplicate field by @serde_json, while repeated keys inside a @BTreeMap
    object resolve last-wins per @serde_json map semantics.

Returns:
  Serialization output is the HTTP bodies ./server.rs serves as `application/json` through
    @axum::Json: @ClusterInfo, @PackagesState, @PopularityContest and a @Vec<@ChildWithState>; every
    struct renders declaration-ordered keys, empty @Vec as `[]`, empty @BTreeMap as `{}`, @None as
    explicit `null`.
  @ScrubStats renders body-embedded as `{"distinct":N,"occurrences":M}`; for the
    state / config / log endpoints ./server.rs instead renders it as the `X-Diag-Redactions` header
    and the payload itself leaves this file as YAML or text.

Raises:
  Nothing — the file holds no functions. Wire failures stay in the caller lane as @serde_json
    errors originating from these derives: missing required key (the message names the field), float
    / negative / numeric-string against @u32 or @usize, wrong type against a scalar, @Vec,
    @BTreeMap or the @Children object, duplicate struct field keys.

Handles:
  Arbitrary content inside @ChildWithState.state — any JSON tree passes through schema-free; only
    the ./collect/ producers and ./anonymize.rs scrubbing constrain what actually arrives.
  Unconstrained text in @PackageState.kind, @tag and every @String field — stored and re-emitted
    verbatim, never trimmed, parsed or validated here.

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover every scenario below with in-file serde tests — this file has no tests today: declaration
      order with explicit `null` rendering, the camelCase @ChildWithState island, @PopularityContest
      byte-stability, @ScrubStats::default() rendering, the accept side (omitted / `null` / unknown
      keys) and the reject side (missing required key, duplicate struct key, `1.5`, `-1`, `"5"` on
      the counters).
  [?] @AnonymizedResponse<@T> is dead code — never constructed workspace-wide, unparseable inbound
      (no @Deserialize), and the redaction contract actually ships as @ScrubStats plus the
      `X-Diag-Redactions` header in ./server.rs. Decide later whether to retire the envelope or make
      an endpoint serve it as body.
  [?] The mixed casing inside one @ChildWithState object — snake_case outer keys, camelCase
      `apiVersion` from @common::Children under `child` — forces clients to parse two conventions in
      the same payload. Decide later whether the server should carry its own snake_case child DTO.
  [?] Count widths are unfixed: @u32 popularity counts versus @usize scrub counters, whose accepted
      JSON range is target-width dependent, so one payload can parse on a 64-bit build yet not a
      32-bit one. Decide later whether both should be fixed-width.
  [?] @PackageState.kind stays a free-form @String discriminator — nothing stops a producer shipping
      a typo on the wire. Decide later whether it becomes an enum.

Done when:
  Every Scenario has a mapped passing test, the Tasks coverage entry is closed and its `[?]`
    decisions recorded, and `cargo test -p server` with clippy and fmt stays green.

Scenario: ClusterInfo renders null for every absent optional
  Given a @ClusterInfo of one @NodeInfo whose four optional facts are @None, @vynil_version @None
    and empty @storage_classes / @ingress_classes
  When @serde_json serializes it
  Then the object is `{"nodes":[{…,"instance_type":null,"arch":null,"os":null,"kubelet_version":null}],"distribution":"…","kubernetes_version":"…","vynil_version":null,"storage_classes":[],"ingress_classes":[]}` —
    declaration order, snake_case, no key skipped
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: ChildWithState nests a camelCase Children under a snake_case key
  Given a @ChildWithState whose @child has @api_version and @namespace @None with kind `Deployment`
    and name `web`, and @state @None
  When it serializes
  Then the exact bytes are `{"child":{"apiVersion":null,"kind":"Deployment","name":"web","namespace":null},"state":null}`
  And deserializing that object back requires `kind` and `name` inside `child` and yields the same
    tree
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Counters reject non-integers
  Given a popularity payload with package count `1.5`, `-1` or `"5"`, and a @ScrubStats payload with
    `distinct` as `"1"`
  When @serde_json deserializes @PopularityContest and @ScrubStats
  Then every one is an invalid-type error — no coercion, no silent zero
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Missing required key names the field
  Given a @ClusterInfo payload holding every key except `distribution`
  When it deserializes
  Then the @serde_json error names the missing field, while the same payload may still omit
    `vynil_version` without failing
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: PopularityContest renders byte-identical regardless of insertion order
  Given two @PopularityContest carrying the same jukebox, category and package set inserted in
    different orders
  When both serialize
  Then the JSON bytes are identical — `jukeboxes`, `categories` and package keys sorted at all
    three map levels
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: AnonymizedResponse is one-way
  Given an @AnonymizedResponse<@PackagesState> with empty @items, @distinct `1` and @occurrences `2`
  When it serializes
  Then the JSON is `{"data":{"items":[]},"scrub_stats":{"distinct":1,"occurrences":2}}`
  And no deserialization of that text into @AnonymizedResponse exists in the crate — `data` and
    `scrub_stats` can only be re-read as separate hand-parsed shapes
  No mapped test exists.

Example:
  @PackagesState body: `{"items":[{"kind":"SystemInstance","namespace":"vynil-system","name":"longhorn","package":"longhorn","tag":"1.3.2","ready":false}]}` —
    `tag` renders `null` when the instance status carries no tag
  @PopularityContest body: `{"jukeboxes":{"longhorn":{"categories":{"storage":{"longhorn":3}}}}}`
  @ChildWithState body: `[{"child":{"apiVersion":"apps/v1","kind":"Deployment","name":"web","namespace":"tenant-a"},"state":{"ready":true}}]`
  @ScrubStats::default() body `{"distinct":0,"occurrences":0}`; the same value in ./server.rs is the
    header `X-Diag-Redactions: distinct=0;occurrences=0` — the serde keys and the header grammar
    share names by literal copy, not by serde
